  "term": "Sjögren–Larsson syndrome",
  "definition": "Sjögren–Larsson syndrome is a rare inherited neurocutaneous disorder that involves congenital ichthyosis along with spastic paraplegia and impaired intellectual development. The packet also states that it is autosomal recessive and is caused by a gene mutation affecting fatty alcohol metabolism.",
